    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the full suite is green (281 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, I added a capacity check that rejects owner creation with **400 Bad Request** when the owner's city already contains 8 owners:\n\n- New guard in `addOwner` (after the daily-registration-limit check):\n  ```java\n  if (cityAtCapacity(owner.getCity())) {\n      return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n  }\n  ```\n- New helper `cityAtCapacity(String city)` with `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 8`. It counts existing owners in the same city **ignoring letter case** (consistent with the surrounding `resolveCity`/`nextCustomerCode` logic) and returns `true` once the count reaches 8. A `null` city is treated as no city (never at capacity).\n\nOnly the V1 controller creates owners; V2 has no `addOwner`, so no change was needed there. All 281 tests pass.",
